  "query_preview": "..There will be little change over the coming week\nwith hot temperatures and low to medium level monsoon activity\ncontinuing. A strong high pressure system aloft will remain \ncentered over New Mexico and Colorado through Wednesday and then \nslowly shift westward over Arizona and Utah by next Saturday.\n\nWidespread cloud cover and light showers have lingered overnight\nacross much of northern Arizona. While modest moisture and\ninstability remains in place today, overall activity does not look\nany more involved than yesterday. The HREF favors the most \nthunderstorm coverage to be over the White Mountains into New\nMexico this afternoon. More isolated activity with gusty outflows will\nthen spread into the lower elevations. An Extreme Heat Warning \nremains in effect through 8PM MST for the elevations below 4000 \nfeet from the Grand Canyon northeastward to Page.\n\nMonsoon moisture will remain in place this week, though slightly\nfade later in the week as the strong, hot high pressure peaks. \nLook for isolated to scattered showers and thunderstorms each day.\nThe mountains will tend to see the first activity by late in the \nmorning where storms will be scattered. Later in the afternoon \nthunderstorms will move into the valleys and generally be more \nisolated. Additional Extreme Heat Warnings are likely to come.",
